[
  "Data addressing by level. Frames are tagged A (outermost) .. D (innermost); the root is ROOT. A level lands on the frame ceil(N/2) climbs above the current one and clamps to the root beyond the outermost frame, so [[1]] and [[2]] name the same frame, as do [[3]] and [[4]]. The grid runs to level 9 at every depth because it is the record of a cell-by-cell cross-check against json-logic-engine; the rows past the first clamp are deliberately repetitive.",
